"content": "<style>\nh1.thlex-title { font-size: 1.3em; margin: 0 0 0.4em; }\n.thlex-key { color: #888; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: normal; margin-right: 0.4em; }\nnav.thlex-index { margin: 0.5em 0 0.75em; }\nnav.thlex-index ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; }\nnav.thlex-index li { margin: 0.15em 0; font-size: 0.95em; }\n.thlex-section { margin: 0.6em 0; }\nh2.thlex-heading { font-size: 1em; margin: 0.5em 0 0.2em; }\nh3.thlex-subheading { font-size: 0.95em; font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; margin: 0.2em 0; }\n.thlex-language-sets { margin: 0.3em 0 0.3em 1em; }\n.thlex-language-set { margin: 0.4em 0; padding-left: 0.75em; border-left: 3px solid #e0e0e0; }\n.thlex-language { font-size: 0.8em; color: #888; margin-right: 0.4em; }\n.thlex-lemma { font-weight: bold; font-family: serif; }\n.thlex-translit { color: #555; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.9em; margin-left: 0.3em; }\n.thlex-refs { font-size: 0.85em; color: #444; margin-top: 0.15em; }\n.thlex-paragraphs p { margin: 0.35em 0; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.5; }\n.thlex-image { margin: 0.5em 0; display: block; }\n.thlex-image img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }\nfigcaption.thlex-caption { font-size: 0.85em; color: #555; font-style: italic; margin-top: 0.2em; }\n.thlex-abbr { border-bottom: 1px dotted #888; cursor: help; }\n.thlex-xref { color: #1a5fb4; }\ntable.thlex-table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9em; margin: 0.5em 0; }\ntable.thlex-table td { padding: 0.2em 0.6em; vertical-align: top; border: 1px solid #ddd; }\ntable.thlex-table tr:first-child td { font-weight: bold; background: #f5f5f5; }\nul.thlex-index-list { margin: 0.4em 0; padding-left: 1.4em; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.6; }\nul.thlex-index-list ul { margin: 0.1em 0; padding-left: 1.4em; }\n.thlex-index-key { font-weight: bold; font-style: italic; }\n</style><h1 class=\"thlex-title\" id=\"REALIA:6.13.1\"><span class=\"thlex-key\">6.13.1</span> 标题：皮条、带子（straps）</h1><div class=\"thlex-section\">\n<h2 class=\"thlex-heading\">经文出处</h2>\n<div class=\"thlex-language-sets\">\n<div class=\"thlex-language-set\">\n<span class=\"thlex-language\">Hebrew</span> <span class=\"thlex-lemma\">来：שְׂרוֹךְ</span> <span class=\"thlex-translit\">(音译：srok)</span>\n<div class=\"thlex-refs\"><data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"01014023\" data-end-ref=\"01014023\">GEN 14:23</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"23005027\" data-end-ref=\"23005027\">ISA 5:27</data></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"thlex-language-set\">\n<span class=\"thlex-language\">Greek</span> <span class=\"thlex-lemma\">希：ἱμάς</span> <span class=\"thlex-translit\">(音译：himas)</span>\n<div class=\"thlex-refs\"><data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"41001007\" data-end-ref=\"41001007\">MRK 1:7</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"42003016\" data-end-ref=\"42003016\">LUK 3:16</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"43001027\" data-end-ref=\"43001027\">JHN 1:27</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"44022025\" data-end-ref=\"44022025\">ACT 22:25</data></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div><div class=\"thlex-section\">\n<h2 class=\"thlex-heading\">描述和用途</h2>\n<div class=\"thlex-paragraphs\">\n<p>皮条是窄而薄的长条皮革，有很多用途，包括系凉鞋、捆东西等（用途类似绳子；参<a class=\"thlex-xref\" data-bnType=\"lexiconLink\" data-collection=\"\" data-key=\"\" href=\"#\">1.14 绳、带 (rope, cord)&lt;REALIA:1.14&gt;</a> ），或者当作鞭子使用（<a class=\"thlex-xref\" data-bnType=\"lexiconLink\" data-collection=\"\" data-key=\"\" href=\"#\">1.1.3 鞭子 (whip, scourge)&lt;REALIA:1.1.3&gt;</a> ）。参看<a class=\"thlex-xref\" data-bnType=\"lexiconLink\" data-collection=\"\" data-key=\"\" href=\"#\">6.13 凉鞋、鞋 (sandal, shoe)&lt;REALIA:6.13&gt;</a> 中的插图。</p>\n<hr/>\n</div>\n</div><div class=\"thlex-section\">\n<h2 class=\"thlex-heading\">翻译</h2>\n<div class=\"thlex-paragraphs\">\n<p>在许多语言中，希腊文<em>himas</em> 可以译为“皮绳”或“皮带”。然而，在<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"43001027\" data-end-ref=\"43001027\">JHN 1:27</data> 中，翻译者可以不译出这个词，而是把意思蕴含在整个句子里面；例如译为，“我不配给他解开凉鞋”（暗指解开系住凉鞋的带子）。<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"41001007\" data-end-ref=\"41001007\">MRK 1:7</data> 和<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"42003016\" data-end-ref=\"42003016\">LUK 3:16</data> 也可以这样处理。</p>\n<p>在<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"44022025\" data-end-ref=\"44022025\">ACT 22:25</data> 中，希腊文<em>himas</em> 可能有两个意思。路加可能是想告诉我们保罗被捆绑的原因，也可能是捆绑的方式。因此，翻译者可以把这节经文的第一个分句翻译成，“他们用皮条把他捆起来”，或者“他们把他捆起来，要鞭打他”，在后面这种情况下，<em>himas</em> 指的是事件，而不是物件。</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
